-- title:
--   Left-unit identity for a pinned addition morphism
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integral domain and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ which is elliptic. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 3, R)$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $W$, with its structure morphism $\pi \colon E \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ (the canonical map to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part, composed with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to (\text{degree }0)$), and let $\mathcal{A}_i$ denote the homogeneous localisation of that quotient away from the class of $X_i$. Let $m \colon E \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} E \to E$ be a morphism such that $m$ followed by $\pi$ equals the first projection followed by $\pi$, and suppose $m$ is pinned in the following sense: for all $i, j \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$ and all $l \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$, the composite of the localisation map $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathcal{A}_i \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_j$ away from `kw_lrSixU W i j l` into $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{A}_i \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_j)$, the inverse of the isomorphism identifying the $(i,j)$ member of the product open cover of $E \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} E$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{A}_i \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_j)$, the open immersion of that member, and $m$, equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l` (on the summand $\mathrm{inl}\ k$, $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `kw_lrChart_tensor` followed by the affine chart inclusion $\operatorname{Proj}$-$\mathrm{away}$ at $X_k$; on $\mathrm{inr}\ k$, the same with `kw_lrSymChart_tensor`). Then the morphism $E \to E \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} E$ with components $\pi$ followed by the zero section `kwZeroSect R W` and the identity of $E$, composed with $m$, is the identity of $E$.
--
--   This is the left-unit axiom $m(O, x) = x$, as a universal identity of scheme morphisms, for an addition morphism on the projective Weierstrass model pinned on the Lange–Ruppert opens of the chart-wise description of the product. It is one of the identities used by [`WeierstrassProjModel.exists_relativeGroupLaw_mul_eq_one_eq_zeroSect_of_addMorphism_sixU_pin`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.exists_relativeGroupLaw_mul_eq_one_eq_zeroSect_of_addMorphism_sixU_pin) and [`WeierstrassProjModel.relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_addMorphism_sixU_pin`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_addMorphism_sixU_pin) to exhibit the relative group law on the model.
